{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/989643-how-much-chemicals-do-you-need-to-kill-a-garou","id":989643,"title":"How much chemicals do you need to kill a garou?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-18T18:15:33-07:00","id":989643,"title":"How much chemicals do you need to kill a garou?","content":"So, i been working on a fomori who can inyect Sodium Thiopental , pancuronium bromide and potassium Chloride (Lethal Inyection) . So i been thinking, other than the &quot;Inmune to toxin's&quot; gift, how much would it take to take down a crinos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T20:53:09-07:00","id":989704,"title":"","content":"There are already pretty broad mechanics for representing poisons, but for shits and giggles, you could always look up the LD50 values of those chemicals and compare them to Crinos weight. The end result will typically be &quot;a lot&quot;, because Crinos weighs at least 150 kg, and is far more likely to be double or even triple that. In some cases, you may need more than reasonably fits in a syringe, or to take steps to make it more concentrated in solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T20:55:46-07:00","id":989705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/989643-how-much-chemicals-do-you-need-to-kill-a-garou#post989643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, i been working on a fomori who can inyect Sodium Thiopental , pancuronium bromide and potassium Chloride (Lethal Inyection) . So i been thinking, other than the &amp;quot;Inmune to toxin's&amp;quot; gift, how much would it take to take down a crinos?</div> </div> </div> </div>Poisons generally have an amount of damage they do. So you have to decide on the damage amount. <br /> If they're in Homid, not too much, though they will death frenzy. In crinos, assume enough to kill a hefty large animal (rhino or large bear?) dead in its tracks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T09:57:55-07:00","id":989928,"title":"","content":"You are kind of doing it backwards.<br /> You don't need to know the number of your villains' shoe sizes.<br /> <br /> Rather than look for a specific 'X number of grams' where X is enough to kill the average Crinos, just say the mockery injects enough to kill/cripple a Crinos werewolf and have it do a lot of damage accompanied by searing pain, wild heart arrhythmia and spasms. Unless your players are taking the damn thing out back and milking it, figuring out the precise dosage is a bit silly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}